title: Aris_Recruitment
---
===
Aris_Intro
===

Aris: A Walker, in my archives. I had hoped you would come.
Aris: I am Aris, the Rooted's archivist. I have preserved what remains of human knowledge — before the Rust, before the Signal, before everything.

-> You remember the old world? That's invaluable.
    === Aris_Knowledge ===
-> The Rooted keep you locked in here with old books?
    === Aris_Choice ===
-> I need to understand the Signal. Can you help?
    === Aris_Signal ===

===
Aris_Knowledge
===

Aris: I was born before the Rust. I have seen civilization rise, fall, and rise again in fragments.
Aris: My body is weak, but my mind holds the blueprint of humanity.

<<set $aris_loyalty = $aris_loyalty + 10>>

-> I'll protect you. Share what you know.
    === Aris_Accepted ===

===
Aris_Choice
===

Aris: I choose preservation over destruction. The Rooted understand that knowledge outlives any war.
Aris: But I confess... I grow tired of walls. I want to see the world I've only read about.

<<set $aris_loyalty = $aris_loyalty + 15>>

-> Then come with me. See it for real.
    === Aris_Accepted ===

===
Aris_Signal
===

Aris: The Signal predates ORACLE. I have records from before the fall — transmissions that match its frequency.
Aris: Something sent the Signal long before ORACLE was built. I believe... the Signal is calling to something. Not warning. Calling.

<<set $aris_loyalty = $aris_loyalty + 20>>

-> That changes everything. You need to come with me.
    === Aris_Accepted ===

===
Aris_Accepted
===

Aris: Very well. I will accompany you. My legs are slow, but my mind is swift.
Aris: Let us discover what the Signal truly is.

<<set $aris_loyalty = 30>>
<<set $aris_recruited = true>>
<<set $active_companions += 1>>
<<set $party: "Aris" = true>>
<<set $quest_aris_library = "active">>

Aris <<companion_join>>
<<give_item bio_gel>>

-> Welcome, archivist. Let's write history together.
    === Aris_Joined ===

===
Aris_Joined
===

Aris: History is written by those who survive. Let us survive. <<signal>>
    -> Agreed. (End)
